{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And He said: You shall not, etc.</b> Meaning: not that I am withholding the thing from you, but rather because you lack the capacity to grasp it, for a man shall not see Me, and His saying <b>and live</b> means: and remain alive, and I am concerned for your life, along the lines of what was said (Psalms 84:11): ״כִּי טוֹב יוֹם בַּחֲצֵרֶיךָ מֵאָלֶף״." "Or it may be said in this manner: <b>for a man shall not see Me</b> — meaning, in any manner whatsoever, and even <b>and live</b> — meaning, even if he be a righteous man who is called חַי (alive), along the lines of what was said (II Samuel 23:20): ״בֶּן אִישׁ חַי״, and the letter vav in וָחָי will serve as the supplemental vav." "It further intends along this line: <b>for a man shall not see Me</b> — even after death, and you seek to see — and further <b>and live</b> — meaning, during the vitality of your life. Here is a hint that after death one may grasp what no man grasped while in the world, for He negated it only on account of his being alive; and even though the righteous gaze upon His light, blessed be He, after their death, they will not grasp what Moses asked from before HaShem. Happy is one born of woman!"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:31.326518090Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}